@api = http://localhost:5180

### Indexed films and configured models
GET {{api}}/movies/stats

### Plot only: Back to the Future ranks 1st
POST {{api}}/movies/search
Content-Type: application/json

{ "description": "a teenager goes back to the 1950s in a time machine car and must reunite his future parents", "top": 5 }

### Plot only: search alone ranks The Terminator 4th (0.739), behind three cyborg films (0.785, 0.756, 0.747)
POST {{api}}/movies/search
Content-Type: application/json

{ "description": "a cyborg assassin is sent back in time to kill the woman whose unborn son will lead humanity", "top": 5 }

### Same question to the assistant: the chat model reads the candidates and picks The Terminator
POST {{api}}/movies/ask
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "a cyborg assassin is sent back in time to kill the woman whose unborn son will lead humanity", "mode": "tool" }

### Plot + criteria: The Goonies
POST {{api}}/movies/search
Content-Type: application/json

{ "description": "kids find an old treasure map and hunt for a pirate's hidden treasure while criminals chase them", "releasedFrom": 1980, "releasedTo": 1989, "genre": "adventure", "top": 5 }

### Brute force vs pgvector index vs index + filter: The Matrix
POST {{api}}/movies/search/compare
Content-Type: application/json

{ "description": "a hacker discovers that the world he lives in is a computer simulation", "releasedFrom": 1990, "releasedTo": 1999, "genre": "science fiction" }

### Agent, context mode: TextSearchProvider searches with the raw question before every call
POST {{api}}/movies/ask
Content-Type: application/json

{ "question": "which late 90s film has a hacker who discovers that reality is a computer simulation?", "mode": "context" }

### 400: domain rule broken
POST {{api}}/movies/search
Content-Type: application/json

{ "description": "a hacker discovers that reality is a simulation", "releasedFrom": 2000, "releasedTo": 1990 }
